# Protocol 02: Document Ingestion and Storage

## Purpose

Receive, classify, preserve and index JSONs, Markdown contracts, audits,
amendments and references. **Ingest before implementing.**

### Intake

For every source: read it; identify purpose; classify authority;
identify entities, dependencies, references and version; detect
conflicts; choose repository location; preserve original; register it;
then decide readiness.

Classes: canonical contract, canonical structured data, audit,
amendment/correction, reference/evidence, implementation artifact,
unknown.

Never silently rewrite originals. Normalized/derived files must retain
explicit provenance.

### Recommended structure

``` text
/
├── AGENTS.md
├── protocols/
├── specs/{foundations,tokens,components,patterns,flows}/
├── sources/{inventories,audits,amendments,references}/
├── registry/{contracts,sources,implementations,qa,decisions,environment}.md
├── implementations/{figma,web}/
├── qa/
└── graphify-out/
```

Canonical contracts/data belong under `specs/`. Audits report evidence
but do not automatically redefine the system. Amendments explicitly
authorize/record changes and must link to affected sources. References
inform but do not govern.

### Current token baseline

The supplied corrected inventory has 270 variables across primitive and
semantic collections. Its adjustment report records conservative
corrections based on demonstrable structure or observable Figma bindings
and leaves unresolved observations unchanged. Once approved in the
project, recommended paths are:
`specs/tokens/tokens.inventory.corrected.json`
`sources/amendments/tokens.audit.adjustments.md`

Do not delete superseded history.

### Registry

Record at least: id, title, path, type, status, authority, version,
received_from, supersedes, superseded_by, depends_on, related_to,
implementation_targets, notes.

Before `READY`, check token, typography, asset, component, pattern,
state, accessibility, behavior and tooling dependencies. Missing
dependency =\> `BLOCKED`.

Conflicts are never silently merged. Apply AGENTS authority; unresolved
conflicts become `CONFLICT`.

Prefer names such as `button.contract.md`, `modal.contract.md`,
`tokens.inventory.corrected.json`. SDD is the methodology, not the file
type.

`INDEXED` means role, authority, location, provenance, dependencies,
conflicts and registry state are known.
